  "body": "## Scope and dependency\n\nDepends on draft #357 (881882e15cd1b2400cc2e0452ea50683dea675de). Repairs the two missing onboarding exports that blocked the complete application typecheck. Reuses canonical server evidence and SessionProvider reconciliation; removes obsolete local signup markers, coalesces reconnects, rejects stale session receipts and retains Party-scoped intent recovery. WO-01\u201305 map to a bounded TLA+ model and component/API tests. No second event or onboarding domain.\n\n## Verification\n\nContract and full pinned TLC/Alloy runner passed before implementation: new model 883 generated / 179 distinct states, depth 7; all 23 expected negative controls detected; two SAT Alloy scenarios and 11 UNSAT assertions within documented bounds. Final focused regression: 9 suites / 77 tests passed. Whole-web application typecheck, focused ESLint, repository quality, staged heuristic audit, shell syntax and 93 documentation links passed. The stable PR-357 backend compile-only rerun also finished successfully; this is not a full backend test-suite pass.\n\n## Global gates remain red \u2014 not merge-ready\n\nFull Jest reported failures in unchanged CourseRegistrationsAdminPage tests, then ceased producing new suite results while consuming CPU; only that run was interrupted (exit 130). No completed aggregate test count is claimed. Full ESLint failed with three errors in unchanged ArtistPublicPage intent/follow and FanHubPage follow code. Vite transformed 12,440 modules, but the existing bundle gate rejected 420,604 gzip bytes versus 419,840 allowed. No test, lint rule, bundle limit or CI control was weakened. Mobile, browser E2E, external analytics and full event workflows remain unverified/incomplete.\n\n## Schema, security and rollback\n\nNo backend, schema, migration, API/generated-client, mobile pointer, feature-flag, permission or provider changes. Signup itself never claims first-value completion. Rollback is reverting this bounded commit, which restores the known broken imports; no data rollback is needed. In-flight coalescing is effect-local; hung requests, cross-tab synchronization and lossless analytics receipts remain limitations. Existing production/legal/accounting/provider gates remain in force. No merge, deployment, provider activation or real-money operation.\n\nExact commands, failure evidence, assumptions, traceability and remaining steps: [PR-15 delivery report](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/827d745629f8cdbaee4429ded3689d3bf520a09d/docs/event-operations/pr-15-web-onboarding-integration.md).",
